From: Edward Wiles <emmabenzvi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 01:30:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Part II.1: expanded D=4 CM-C+ equivalence battery (60/60
 pass)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the D=4 gate with categories the brief calls out specifically:
every free coordinate individually (all 15 A-block coords), 8 fixed
bandwidths, top-3-fast-path vs generic-full-rescan-fallback isolation
(both backends, cross-checked), forced exact price ties (both builders
throw TiedWinnerError identically), controlled near-ties swept across 14
(sign,eps) combinations, an explicitly constructed incumbent-swap point,
a nonfinite-probe/retry-discipline check, and a zero-multiplier-column
survey (none found naturally, disclosed rather than fabricated).

Root-caused and fixed a real bug in this session's OWN near-tie test
construction (not a CM-C+ defect): merge(ctx, (U=Unear,)) alone leaves
ctx.γ.Uσ (a precomputed derivative of U built once at setup time) stale,
causing Reference's dense pTσ path and C+'s log-score path to disagree by
~6e-2 -- a discrepancy that persisted UNCHANGED across eps=1e-2 down to
1e-8, which is itself the tell that it wasn't genuine near-tie
sensitivity. Isolated via diag_near_tie_isolate.jl (kept as supporting
evidence): recomputing γ.Uσ = Unew.^(1-σ) alongside U drops the
discrepancy to 1e-15. Added ctx_with_U(ctx, Unew) helper so both the
forced-tie and near-tie sections construct consistent contexts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
